 ## Background
-The Möller-Trumbore algorithm was published by Tomas Möller and Ben Trumbore in the article "Fast, Minimum Storage Ray-Triangle Intersection" (Aug 2005) [S5, unofficial]. It is used in volume rendering pipelines to determine entry and exit distances (sampling intervals) for triangles [S3, unofficial]. It is referenced in implementations such as GPView [S1, unofficial].
